{
  "_doc": "Founding cast of the 100-resident town (Phase 016a; reshaped in Phase 016b).\n\nFOUNDING_JOBS: one row per JOBS key (frames/jobs.json). The founding cast takes its roles and counts from E.seed_jobs(100): each resident's role is the first job that seed gives them. This table holds only what a job needs beyond the JOBS data: group (the class and station tier, a FOUNDING_CLASS.by_group key), role_identity_mean and role_identity_sd (the drawn role-identity of holders), and workplace (a FOUNDING_WORKPLACES key, a FOUNDING_DEPOSITS kind, or 'farm'). Every value is an authored design choice, not a census figure (APPROX). The workplace of the jobs with no workshop anchor in FOUNDING_WORKPLACES (smith, cooper, tailor, weaver, leatherworker, butcher, dairymaid, animal_keeper) reuses the nearest existing anchor; adding anchors would change the founding map (a follow-up, see PHASE016B_REPORT.md).\n\nFOUNDING_AGE: the founders' ages (years). A clipped Normal on its own seed stream (seed + stream). Bounds are the adult life stage (LIFE_STAGES.adult: 18 to 64). The mean and sd are APPROX: a working-age adult population of a pre-industrial village, not a measured age structure.\n\nFOUNDING_CLASS.by_group: each group's [rich, middle] shares; poor is the remainder (authored, APPROX). literacy_by_class: the chance of literacy by class (authored, APPROX). station_by_group: the STATION_EDUCATION key of each group (as populate_town100 used it). capability_by_literacy: the general capability of a literate and an unlettered founder (the values populate_town100 used at HEAD; authored, APPROX, not sourced).\n\nFOUNDING_ANCHOR_NAMES: job -> the register name of the first resident with that job. 'fishmonger' keeps the register name of the fishmonger role of 016a (Doreen Ferrety); the fishmonger job is a fixed-load shop job added to JOBS in 016b (trade: fisher), and the reporter job (trade: reporter, workplace press) too. The banker anchor (Scrooge) was dropped: the banker role has no JOBS entry, so no resident could hold the name.\nFOUNDING_DRAW_BOUNDS.role_identity: the clip range of the role-identity draw.",
